************ SPECIAL FORMATTED COMMENT **********
EW API FORMATTED COMMENT
TYPE LIBRARY

LIBRARY  EWDB_APPLICATIONS

SUB_LIBRARY reaper

LOCATION THIS_FILE

LINK_NAME Sample Config File
LINK reaper.d.txt

DESCRIPTION <b>reaper</b> is a catch-all, database cleanup program.
It deletes all parametric, waveform, and strong motion data from
the database that is more than X days old, where X is the value set
for <DaysTillReckoning> in the config file. <br><br>  
<b>(Nothing survives the reaper!)</b>.  It deletes data based
on both Origin time of events and also timestamps for unassociated
data.  The functionality of the <b>reaper</b> is a subset of db_cleanup2.
It does not do archiving, and it deletes all data older than a given number
of days.  <br><br>
This program is meant to be run out of cron(or some other 
periodic invocation method). Its function is to keep the 
amount of data in the database manageable, by deleting the
oldest data.  This is done so that the database
doesn't fill-up or incur problems because of data build-up over time.
<br><br> 
Adapted from <b>db_cleanup</b>.
Initial version by DavidK 2001/07/14


